  "header": "A shared training opt-out is coming. It is not on yet.",
  "friendlyHeader": "Websites may soon share one training opt-out. It is not switched on yet.",
  "summary": "On 30 October, OpenAI and Google said they will honor one robots.txt signal for AI training, so a site does not have to write a separate rule for every crawler. Neither company has switched it on. The rest of today's issue is about the limits that already apply: a cyber-access session that can still be used for training, a renamed Claude plan, and a delivery company that has counted only a few hundred orders from outside agents.",
  "friendlySummary": "On 30 October, OpenAI and Google said they will follow one shared file setting that tells AI companies not to train on a website. Neither company has turned that setting on. Today also covers a special ChatGPT session that can still be used for training, a renamed Claude plan, and a food-delivery company that has seen only a few hundred orders from outside AI agents.",
